            <div xml:id="d339">

                <pb facs="0429" n="417" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg417"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.0090/22: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-05-07">May 7, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1160. Department’s 879, April 7, paragraph 10. Department now informed that <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gripsholm</hi> cannot leave Sweden before May 25 and
                    will possibly be delayed until May 30. Accordingly vessel will be unable to
                    depart from United States until June 10 to 15 arriving at Lourenço Marques 1
                    month later. Swiss representatives Par East should be informed urgently and
                    requested to communicate this information to Department’s officers.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
